Z||000025||Cooter||06-18-2000||02:17 PM||||I just email from "the Man himself":<P>From Archie:<BR>Just for the record, I was driving V-8 Fieros for nearly a year before I became a supplier.  So, in this conversation, as it applies to me, "driver" and "supplier" could be considered interchangeable terms.<P>I read the post very carefully & I would think that a teacher could see that the specific terms you mention really have no impact on the message I was conveying.  That would be true, unless you didn't know my history. If you didn't know my history, you shouldn't have posted until you did your "homework".  Maybe you could do your research before shooting off at the mouth.   <P>I have a friend who is a teacher, many times he's too busy editing the grammar to hear the message.<P>I'm posting this as a private message because that is what you should have done.  You really don't want to step into this thread if you don't have your facts straight.<P>Try being nice next time.<P>Archie<P>Well, now I have decided that the 3.8 is going into my project car and it will never see a V-8 Archie kit. Thanks for saving me some money smart guy.<P>Greg||||reg||1
