Z||000035||Spyder||06-18-2000||05:23 PM||||On other boards I have seen Archie being <BR>"Attacked Verbally And Threatened" <BR>by some people, so that is why he so quickly responds in the tone he does.<P>I bought my V8 kit from Archie. <BR>I did my research on what was available and called around and figured what was best for me. <BR>I called Archie and he answered all my questions.<BR>He was straight up and honest with me.<BR>He even sent me an installation video on building a 308 kit car, I was building a <BR>328 and had no instructions at all. He took the time to make a copy and didn't even charge me for it.<BR>I am thoroughly pleased with the V8 installation.<BR>I have never had any problems with Archie AT ALL.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000036||Cooter||06-18-2000||05:39 PM||||Okay, I'm sorry, I'm finished here. Let's move on now.||||reg||1
Z||000037||stimpy||06-18-2000||05:44 PM||||I have never heard any reason that anyone has been dissatisfied with products or services from Archie. And the fact that, as silhouette stated "everyone knows Archie", obiviously shows that he is a high profile member of the community, as such there will be people jealous of his success. In other words, people will always talk sh*t.  <BR>I don't question that this is a guy who has stayed in business because he provides a quality product in a limited marketplace. I still think he is a grouchy old fart though. But don't let that stop ya if you want a V8. ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Archie||06-18-2000||06:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Your right, BAMx2, it's my fault, I admit it. <P>So YOUR the one!!!!<P>BTW, I am not the most well versed person when it comes to netiquette, but isn't posting private email kind of, well, rude? <P>Oh, and Archie- I have a BIGA$$ stereo in my car!!! So obviously I've been kicked off of your board. Welcome to our world. Peace, baby!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I understand that your the funny guy around here, TechNet could use a little humor. A couple of years ago I tried to give them some of my raw humor and everyone was way to serious. Even people with BIGA$$ stereo systems are welcome, they are just asked not to make it the subject of a thread.<P>There has been just one person banned from TechNet & he's not involved in this thread.  A few people have claimed that I booted them off the list.  But in reality, one of them was automatically booted by the server because his EMail address kept bouncing mail back to the server.  Another guy claims his problem was due to dis-agreeing about GT production. He actually was booted because he was sending nasty EMails to other members off-list. So maybe there are a few facts being omited by some of your Vendor Bashers.<P>BTW, I would like to say one more thing.....I was a Fiero enthusiast before most of you guys got out of Grade School. I, like most other Fiero owners, have an opinion on most anything Fiero Related.  Most Fiero Vendors will kiss tons of butt to keep from offending anyone and losing a little business. When a thread like this gets started they will keep thier heads down because they are worried about offending someone.  You know who they are, they are the ones who never make a post that has any hint of expressing an opinion. Well I can't be like that, I am a Fiero Enthusiast FIRST and a Vendor SECOND. I know that is not the thing a business person should say, but I can't let lies and incorrect statements stand. Many times when someone dis-agrees with something I say, they always say something like Cooter said earlier when he said "...and your actions here will be remembered with their wallets". I get sick of hearing that. If the support of my customers, my after the sale Customer support, my products, my reputation and my Internet involvement don't speak enough about my operation then your threats to my business mean nothing.  If you think I'm going to kiss your butt for the possibility that you might someday be a customer, then you need to seek out other Vendors who are used to kissing your butt.<P>Cootie, Good luck on your 3.8 swap.  I'm sure there is a vendor out there who will kiss your butt. I just can't figure why you would try to correct me on some definitions then after I explain my meaning, you come back like some punk High School kid and say "Bite Me." that reveals more about you than your Profile ever will.<P>To those who think I've mis-treated them on TechNet, I say, There are 2 sides to every story, Get over it, grow up.<P>Oh, cool, now Cooter want to move on.  What the heck were you thinking when you stuck your nose in here in the first place?<P>Now I remember why I've been a member for 6 months and have not said anything and only rarely read any of this stuff.<P>Archie||||reg||12
Z||000039||BOILERMAKER||06-18-2000||06:14 PM||||Hmmmm, it seems to me that if Archie would have posted those same statements (that he made on this thread) onto his own site, he would have had to kick himself off (from what I have been told).<P>Nice to see that he can come in here and get edgy with us and we can't have a factual conversation (i.e. 85 GT) on his site.||||reg||1
Z||000040||stimpy||06-18-2000||06:44 PM||||You go with yer bad self Archie!!!! Wooo-hooo! This is more fun then Jerry Springer! <P>Archie, I'm telling ya, come on out of your shell. I'm actually beginning to start to like you!<P>Oh, and Boilermaker, did you read ANY of Archies last post?||||reg||14
